{"id":"qzpyq-chemistry-hydrocarbons-hydrocarbons-test-2","_quizrrTestId":"69de21f57e39d99b57bc5b4d","title":"Hydrocarbons - Test 2","questions":[{"id":"qz_69de4f7e2ee0e063d928f956","_quizrrId":"69de4f7e2ee0e063d928f956","q":"Following are the four molecules \"P\", \"Q\", \"R\" and \"S\".\nWhich one among the four molecules will react with $\\mathrm{H}-\\mathrm{Br}_{(\\mathrm{aq})}$ at the fastest rate?\n<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-book-fc5b54ef391f14ef.png?alt=media&v=stem2\"/ data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-fc5b54ef391f14ef.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-fc5b54ef391f14ef.png\"><br/>","options":["R","P","Q","S"],"answer":2,"answers":[2],"questionType":"singleCorrect","subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Hydrocarbons","exam":"JEE Main","source":"Quantrex PYQ Chapterwise","solution":"Addition of $\\mathrm{H}-\\mathrm{Br}_{(\\mathrm{aq})}$ to alkene follows electrophilic addition mechanism. In the rate determining step a carbocation intermediate is formed. Among $\\mathrm{P}, \\mathrm{Q}$, R \\& S compound Q will form most stable carbocation intermediate since it is resonance stabilized. <img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-book-bb5b47d2b9f02e0e.png?alt=media&v=stem2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-bb5b47d2b9f02e0e.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-bb5b47d2b9f02e0e.png\"><br>","_bank":"quizrr_pyq_chapter","_testId":"69de21f57e39d99b57bc5b4d"},{"id":"qz_69de4f7e2ee0e063d928f95b","_quizrrId":"69de4f7e2ee0e063d928f95b","q":"<p>Given below are two statements.</p><p>Statement I: The presence of weaker $\\pi$-bonds make alkenes less stable than alkanes</p><p>Statement II: The strength of the double bond is greater than that of carbon-carbon single bond.</p><p>In the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options : given below.</p>","options":["Both Statement I and Statement II are correct.","Both Statement I and Statement II are incorrect.","Statement I is correct but Statement II is incorrect.","Statement I is incorrect but Statement II is correct."],"answer":0,"answers":[0],"questionType":"singleCorrect","subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Hydrocarbons","exam":"JEE Main","source":"Quantrex PYQ Chapterwise","solution":"<p>As sigma bond is formed along the internuclear axis it is stronger than pi-bond, and due to the presence of pi-bonds alkenes will be more reactive towards electrophilic reagents.Hence they are less stable than alkanes.</p><p>The strength of carbon-carbon double bond is greater than single bond as bond strength is directly proportional to bond order.</p><p>Hence, both the statements are correct.</p>","_bank":"quizrr_pyq_chapter","_testId":"69de21f57e39d99b57bc5b4d"},{"id":"qz_69de4f7e2ee0e063d928f960","_quizrrId":"69de4f7e2ee0e063d928f960","q":"The major product  \\left[B\\right]$ in the following sequence of reactions is:<br /><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-book-66c8d7507dfada93.png?alt=media&v=stem2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-66c8d7507dfada93.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-66c8d7507dfada93.png\">$","options":["<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-book-4ba2fd79630f99cc.png?alt=media&v=stem2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-4ba2fd79630f99cc.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-4ba2fd79630f99cc.png\">","<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-book-a02d8613c927701d.png?alt=media&v=stem2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-a02d8613c927701d.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-a02d8613c927701d.png\">","<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-book-31558e90f4cf5860.png?alt=media&v=stem2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-31558e90f4cf5860.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-31558e90f4cf5860.png\">","<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-book-29ea1d33f81570fa.png?alt=media&v=stem2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-29ea1d33f81570fa.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-29ea1d33f81570fa.png\">"],"answer":1,"answers":[1],"questionType":"singleCorrect","subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Hydrocarbons","exam":"JEE Main","source":"Quantrex PYQ Chapterwise","solution":"<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-book-3673061a802c5e64.png?alt=media&v=stem2\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 300px;\" / data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-3673061a802c5e64.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-3673061a802c5e64.png\"></p><p>Alcohol upon reaction with protic acids tends to lose a molecule of water to form alkenes. These reactions are known as dehydrogenation or dehydration of alcohols. It is an example of an elimination reaction.The order of the ease of dehydration of alcohols is: tertiary &gt; secondary &gt; primary.& </p>","_bank":"quizrr_pyq_chapter","_testId":"69de21f57e39d99b57bc5b4d"},{"id":"qz_69de4f7f2ee0e063d928f965","_quizrrId":"69de4f7f2ee0e063d928f965","q":"<p>Given below are two statements, one is labelled as</p><p><strong>Assertion A</strong> and the other is labelled as& <strong>Reason R.</strong></p><p><strong>Assertion A :</strong> Benzene is more stable than hypothetical cyclohexatriene.</p><p><strong>Reason R :</strong> The delocalized $\\pi$& electron cloud is attracted more strongly by nuclei of carbon atoms.</p><p>In the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below:</p>","options":["A is true but R is false.","A is false but R is true.","Both A and R are correct and R is the correct explanation of A.","Both A and R are correct but R is NOT the correct explanation of A."],"answer":2,"answers":[2],"questionType":"singleCorrect","subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Hydrocarbons","exam":"JEE Main","source":"Quantrex PYQ Chapterwise","solution":"<p>The delocalised $\\pi -$electron cloud is attracted more strongly by the nuclei of the carbon atoms than the electron cloud localised between two carbon atoms. Therefore, presence of delocalised $\\pi -$electrons in benzene makes it more stable than the hypothetical cyclohexatriene.</p>","_bank":"quizrr_pyq_chapter","_testId":"69de21f57e39d99b57bc5b4d"},{"id":"qz_69de4f7f2ee0e063d928f96a","_quizrrId":"69de4f7f2ee0e063d928f96a","q":"<p>The major product of the following reaction is :</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-book-30faf0f29ecb5931.png?alt=media&v=stem2\" style=\"width: 155px; height: 83px;\" / data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-30faf0f29ecb5931.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-30faf0f29ecb5931.png\"></p>","options":["<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-book-d2607dd3de1c56ce.png?alt=media&v=stem2\" style=\"width: 108px; height: 83px;\" / data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-d2607dd3de1c56ce.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-d2607dd3de1c56ce.png\">","<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-book-bca7e69041691b2b.png?alt=media&v=stem2\" style=\"width: 98px; height: 83px;\" / data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-bca7e69041691b2